on and reset determine validity of outstanding confirmation context.\",\n        \"B_client\": \"Origin batch context lookup supplies the downstream consumption dependency.\"\n      },\n      \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n      \"counterevidence\": [\n        \"The local completion branch uses s.ctx correctly.\",\n        \"Confirmation intentionally raises earlier request indices to the latest confirmed index, which can be safe and is not the discrepancy.\",\n        \"Timeout is a permitted client outcome; mismatch must be assessed as an independently grounded correlation duty, not an invented response deadline.\",\n        \"Membership and term filtering protect incoming confirmations.\",\n        \"Later confirmation deliberately releases earlier contexts and may raise their read indices; the existing TestReadIndexLeaderCanBeConfirmed checks that each returned context remains its original context.\",\n        \"Network send failures are allowed, but no success deadline is derived from message loss or recovery.\"\n      ],\n      \"unknowns\": [\n        \"Execute the actual Peer entry, forwarding, heartbeat producer, quorum confirmation and ReadyToRead consumer in one correlated history; source edges alone do not show that history ran.\",\n        \"Confirm the emitted and consumed context at each distinct remote origin without using the compared context as an observation filter.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 0,\n      \"trigger_rationale\": \"readIndex.confirm returns saved statuses for earlier contexts, but the remote response branch encodes m.Hint/m.HintHigh rather than s.ctx, unlike its local branch. Receiving pendingReadIndex.addReady matches exact contexts. Inspecting this concrete producer/consumer difference is more informative than testing arbitrary inputs.\"\n    },\n    \"status\": \"escalated\",\n    \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n    \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n    \"stop_reason\": \"Ground the narrowly scoped remote read-context p